// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/analog/mos_psp103_vsb_data.t27 -- the IHP SG13G2 PSP103 current tables with a source-to-bulk axis, corner mos_tt, 27 C: data, the accessors and the tests of the data
; M3e of the analog emulation epic (#10486, issue #11283). The log-domain tables of mos_psp103_data.t27 (TT_LG_N, TT_LG_P) are Id(Vgs, Vds) of sg13_lv_nmos (W 1.0 um, L 0.45 um) and
; sg13_lv_pmos (W 3.0 um, L 0.45 um) with each bulk tied to its source, so they hold no body effect. A transmission gate has its bulks on the rails (the NMOS on ground, the PMOS on
; the supply) and conducts with its sources between them: while it conducts at 0.75 V the NMOS source is 0.75 V above its bulk and the PMOS source 0.75 V below its bulk, which raises
; both thresholds, and ngspice's real cell is 30 percent above the tables' Ron (mos_psp103_gates.t27, accept_tgate.cir). This file adds the missing axis: the same two tables at
; six more source-to-bulk voltages Vsb = 0.25, 0.5, .. 1.5 V (the slices 1 .. 6; the slice 0 is the existing 2-D table, which is the Vsb = 0 case, so the read at Vsb = 0 is the 2-D
; read bit for bit). The read is in mos_table.t27 (`lg_fine_vsb`, the log word blended between two slices); the accessors here pick the two slices around a Vsb.
; -
; WHERE THE NUMBERS COME FROM. ngspice-47 and the IHP-Open-PDK checkout at commit 21133f219b1a6da10d803e345761e77415ceff40 (cornerMOSlv.lib, PSP 103.6, section mos_tt, psp103.osdi from
; the same commit), 27 C, on the reference host (a container, 2 threads), 2026-10-20, one deck run twice (46 s and 48 s; the data rows of the two logs are identical): specs/analog/decks/psp103_idpa_vsb_tt.cir, psp103_idpa_tt.cir with the
; bulk of each device on its own source of voltage: the NMOS bulk at -Vsb (its source at 0 V), the PMOS bulk at 1.5 V + Vsb (its source at the 1.5 V rail). Vsb is a reverse bias
; for both, a magnitude. The grid, the gate scale s(Vgs) (the tt one, the same at every Vsb, so rv is a function of Vgs only), the encoding (log2(Id / F) in 1/65536 of an octave over
; IUNIT = 1.164 pA, the Vds = 0 column the limit s_eff * gds0) are those of TT_LG_N and TT_LG_P: a slice is a table of 4851 words (the tag word 4294967295, 4753 log words
; at ix * 49 + iy, 97 rv words) that the 2-D reader reads as it reads TT_LG_N. The six slices of the NMOS are VSB_N1 .. VSB_N6 and of the PMOS VSB_P1 .. VSB_P6. The deck also prints
; the slice 0 (Vsb = 0 with the bulk as a node of its own): it agrees with TT_LG_N and TT_LG_P in all but 4 and 3 of 4753 words, by at most 3 and 1 words (3 / 65536 of an octave is
; 0.003 percent of a current), the solver noise of two netlists at reltol 1e-6; it is not pasted, so the accessors take the existing tables for the slice 0.
; -
; THE AXIS. Seven slices 0.25 V apart over 0 .. 1.5 V: the count is what the transmission gate's Ron needs, measured before it was chosen (the same data read with 4 slices, 0.5 V apart,
; is within 0.29 percent of ngspice's real cell at the worst of 27 points, with 7 within 0.09 percent; with 3 (0.75 V apart) 0.58 percent; the bar is 10 percent), and the held-out
; currents between slices keep the read to 2.5 percent (7 slices), 5.8 percent (4) and 14 percent (3): a chord of the log word over a slice is exact where the threshold moves linearly
; with Vsb and is not where it bends (the square-root law is steepest near Vsb = 0). The three counts were read off the same printed tables with a floating-point twin of the reader,
; a scratch run outside the repository, and the integer read of mos_table.t27 is what the tests of mos_psp103_gates.t27 judge.
; -
; THE HELD-OUT POINTS are 1000 currents in pA (nint(Id * 1e12)) at centres of the cells of the 3-D grid, the places a chord of it is worst: point k = 1 .. 1000 is
; Vgs = (floor(96 frac(k a1)) + 1/2) * 15.625 mV, Vds = (floor(48 frac(k a2)) + 1/2) * 31.25 mV, Vsb = (floor(6 frac(k a3)) + 1/2) * 0.25 V (so Vsb is halfway between two slices:
; 0.125, 0.375, .. 1.375 V), a1, a2, a3 = R3_A1, R3_A2, R3_A3 (the 3-D R sequence, 1 / g, 1 / g^2 and 1 / g^3 for g^4 = g + 1). VSB_CEN_N and VSB_CEN_P. They were not used to make a
; table. The pins fail on any changed number.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. The numbers in this file are the numbers the deck printed, in order (the pins); the slices are tables of the format the 2-D reader reads; the rv words are the
; same in every slice; the current of a device falls with Vsb at every node above Vgs = 0.25 V; and the read at Vsb = 0 is the 2-D read of the existing table. WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY.
; That the interpolation along Vsb is accurate (mos_psp103_gates.t27 judges it against the held-out currents and the real tgate), anything about another corner, temperature, W, L or m,
; the leakage floor of the off state (a log word below 1 IUNIT is held at 0, so the PMOS off current at Vsb above 0.5 V is a floor, and the junction leakage that rises with Vsb is
; not resolved below it), or a bulk forward-biased against its source (Vsb below 0). The model is a TABLE MODEL of PSP103, not PSP103. ASCII only, English only.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module AnalogMosPsp103VsbData;

use analog::mos_table::{lg_fine, lg_fine_vsb, lg_vsb_cell, lg_vsb_frac, LG_TAG};
use analog::mos_psp103_data::{TT_LG_N, TT_LG_P, fold_arr};

; --- what the numbers are ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const KIND : str = "analog-table-data";
pub const ID : str = "analog/mos_psp103_vsb_data";
pub const REFERENCE : str = "IHP-Open-PDK ihp-sg13g2 cornerMOSlv.lib (PSP 103.6) through ngspice-47 and OSDI, bulk off the source; deck specs/analog/decks/psp103_idpa_vsb_tt.cir";
/// The IHP-Open-PDK checkout every number was made from (the commit of M3b's tables).
pub const PDK_COMMIT : str = "21133f219b1a6da10d803e345761e77415ceff40";
pub const TEMP_C : u32 = 27;
/// The slices along Vsb (slice 0 is the existing 2-D table), 0.25 V apart, and the held-out points.
pub const VSB_NSLICE : u32 = 7;
pub const VSB_STEP_MV : u32 = 250;
pub const VSB_CEN_COUNT : u32 = 1000;
/// The device index of the accessors: the NMOS table, the PMOS table.
pub const DEV_N : u32 = 0;
pub const DEV_P : u32 = 1;
/// The 3-D R sequence of the held-out points: 1 / g, 1 / g^2, 1 / g^3 for g the real root of g^4 = g + 1.
pub const R3_A1 : f64 = 0.8191725133961645;
pub const R3_A2 : f64 = 0.6710436067037893;
pub const R3_A3 : f64 = 0.5497004779019703;

; --- order-sensitive folds of the pasted numbers (fold_arr of mos_psp103_data.t27) ------------------------------------
/// The twelve slices in the order VSB_N1 .. VSB_N6, VSB_P1 .. VSB_P6 (4851 words each), and the two held-out sets, NMOS then PMOS.
pub const PIN_VSB_LG : u64 = 0x8643D5629A3C357E;
pub const PIN_VSB_CEN : u64 = 0x061EB2F38AC69E0C;

; --- the numbers --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
